==Trivia==
[[File:Death (Doom).webp|thumb|A player dying to the Doom modifier.]]
* Carrying on the Civitas illa Fortis references to Rome, the Fortis Colosseum is based upon the [[wikipedia:Colosseum|Roman Colosseum]], where gladiators and convicts would fight one another and wild animals during the imperial era.
* Roughly 36 hours after release, players had reclaimed items from their graves totaling {{Coins|52673267112}}, with Sol Heredit being killed 101 times and 1,178,295 waves completed.{{CiteTwitter|author=Old School Runescape|url=https://twitter.com/OldSchoolRS/status/1771188690557034834|date=22 March 2024|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/27963378|archivedate=23 March 2024}}
** Within a week of release, players had reclaimed items from their graves totaling {{Coins|155591568214}}, with Sol Heredit being killed 5,763 times and 5,067,964 waves completed.
* The icons for several modifiers resemble Maya logograms (glyphs that represent whole words):
** The icon for Relentless resembles the glyph ''[[commons:File:Balam_1.svg|b'alam]]'', meaning jaguar.
** The icon for Reentry resembles the glyph ''[https://mayaglyphs.org/CWLhtml/K%27UK%27logo.html k'uk']'', meaning quetzal.
** The icon for Dynamic Duo resembles the glyph ''[https://mayaglyphs.org/CWLhtml/%40%7BYUK%7DKAWAK%40logo.html kawak]'', the 19th day of the [[wikipedia:Tzolkʼin|tzolk'in]] calendar.
** The icon for Quartet resembles the glyph ''[https://mayaglyphs.org/CWLhtml/EK%27logo.html ek']'', meaning star.
** The icon for Frailty resembles the glyph ''[https://mayaglyphs.org/CWLhtml/TZ%27I%27logo.html tz'i']''/''[https://mayaglyphs.org/CWLhtml/TZ%27I%27logo.html ok]'', meaning dog.
* Dying to the Doom modifier uses a unique death animation, where the player dissolves into a puddle of acid.

